### Local environment overrides ###
# The backend has no .env file: `src/main/resources/application.properties` is the
# single source of configuration, and secrets reach it as environment variables
# (JWT_SECRET, DB_PASSWORD) rather than through a committed or local env file.
#
# docker compose still reads a `.env` from this directory if one exists, because
# that is how compose interpolates ${...} in docker-compose.yml. It is ignored here
# so an accidentally created one can never be committed with live credentials.
.env
.env.*

